    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Applied at the corners and edges of boxes, high-density foam provides targeted impact resistance. This material typically features a density of 40-50 kg/m³, offering superior energy absorption compared to standard packing paper. In the context of the Chatra to Tori route, where vehicles may encounter uneven surfaces and sudden stops, these foam edges absorb the kinetic energy of impacts, protecting the most vulnerable points of the package from catastrophic breakage.</p>
